  "caption": {
    "text": "Part 4 of ITERATORS & GENERATORS. Most Python devs write `yield` for years without ever seeing what it actually does: it freezes a stack frame on the heap and hands the caller a bookmark. This handbook walks the whole iteration model — iter/next mechanics, hand-rolled iterator classes, generator internals (gi_frame, GeneratorExit, PEP 479), lazy pipelines, itertools, and the silent-zero bugs that only show up in production. Save it for the next time `sum(g)` returns 0 and nothing raises.",
